# This repository is PUBLIC. Everything here is served to a proxy core or client
# over HTTP, so the rule is inverted compared with a normal project: the danger is
# not committing junk, it is committing something that should never have left the
# machine.
#
# Two provenance classes live here and their boundaries are enforced differently:
#
#   mihomo/**        generated by proxykit. The real boundary is that repo's
#                    scripts/sync-assets.sh, which refuses to copy anything
#                    carrying a local absolute path or a credential-shaped key.
#                    If a pattern below ever fires for mihomo/, the script has a
#                    bug -- fix the script rather than relying on this file.
#   quantumult-x/**  hand-written, edited in place. Here these patterns ARE the
#                    boundary, because no script gates them.

# --- credential-bearing files ------------------------------------------------
# QuantumultX: mitm.txt holds the MITM CA private key; release.conf is the real
# profile and carries the [server_remote] subscription URLs. The tracked
# QuantumultX.conf deliberately ships with [server_remote] and [mitm] empty.
#
# These two paths MOVED in the 2026-09-01 reorganisation (Profile/ ->
# quantumult-x/profile/). If you ever move them again, move these lines in the
# same commit -- an ignore pattern left pointing at the old path fails silently,
# and the failure mode is a private key in a public repository.
quantumult-x/profile/mitm.txt
quantumult-x/profile/release.conf

# Merged subscriptions and full profiles carry node credentials (password, uuid,
# server addresses). They are regenerable from the code repo and are deliberately
# not versioned anywhere. The *.yaml/*.yml globs are deliberately broad: a stray
# YAML here is far likelier to be a merged subscription than something worth
# keeping. Use `git add -f` for a legitimate one.
profiles/
subs/
*.yaml
*.yml
!.github/**/*.yml

# --- local-only scratch ------------------------------------------------------
# JS/Debug/ became quantumult-x/js/Debug/ in the same reorganisation. Its three
# files were already tracked before the pattern was added, so they stay tracked;
# the pattern only stops new ones.
quantumult-x/js/Debug/
.vscode/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.DS_Store
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.tmp
